{"title":"2024 USAJMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4f26182ce276bf3f592d12dc9d55b85e97be46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac3714b34cf543a4e1cd0bb979b7bbaa693c3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are selected on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9c15d1345cd315edc92dd38b8708c5ee37ed2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = BQ = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are selected on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd8f31478c67a57b1f2921f6839851edd25dc57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CR = DS = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integer points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd67c3f7417b5d3965610ff48a916a79ec5c33c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq x\\leq2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/27276bb81908fc5372134169a84d11e2a5172aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq y\\leq2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />. A configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150c08478d63c3d2f5cc0de4222ea9183673d7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$mn$\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" /> rectangles is called <i>happy</i> if each point in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a vertex of exactly one rectangle, and all rectangles have sides parallel to the coordinate axes. Prove that the number of <i>happy</i> configurations is odd.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d80cbff7b1da39b3e70a6465ebae587c4629d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> be the sequence defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06215158ce5affca3c27b9ddc883ba73e08f095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa7bca01669da68cc9ba0db05f0c960fb8cfde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(n+1)=(a(n))^{n+1}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" /> for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28324eb1d52d541982598613d2d7ac4cb4e526e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f939f7005de80d9837c6cb9b12317711b634b1fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer. Prove that some term of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d80cbff7b1da39b3e70a6465ebae587c4629d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6585024dc6db82bcfd717e03212be80536d94a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer. Rowan and Colin play a game on an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> grid of squares, where each square is colored either red or blue. Rowan is allowed to permute the rows of the grid, and Colin is allowed to permute the columns of the grid. A grid coloring is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c1c51a8773cf07ff1bce73f34e7d712fd6b89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$orderly$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> if:\n</p>\n<ul><li>no matter how Rowan permutes the rows of the coloring, Colin can then permute the columns to restore the original grid coloring; and</li></ul>\n<ul><li>no matter how Colin permutes the columns of the coloring, Rowan can then permute the rows to restore the original grid coloring;</li></ul>\n<p>In terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, how many orderly colorings are there?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904cf01fc90d3288a1d01c897e21ca7ff5f4a9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdeaa49c29c972b00378da74fa56558da3d543e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x^2-y)+2yf(x)=f(f(x))+f(y)\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\nfor all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5c9755a11dfd9dea1da1dcd236e268bad8675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is selected inside acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acd00d8a9993fe8dbef8619ca092bdcadd29317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC=\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237c8a74e6a9d07badfb12532e8e64f7d9ef2cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC=90^\\circ+\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"16\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc64d695e60b2ce5256f22259d4a9dca7cd7176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Show that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cf35ccd4cc779c3ba0c092b7f6de4bad558ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO\" title=\"2024 USAJMO\">2024 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems\">2023 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems\">2025 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034312\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 292/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 84/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7975/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.846      1 -total\n 55.09%    7.628      1 Template:USAJMO_box\n 43.34%    6.001      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27123:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034312 and revision id 279729. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}